block head
    title Periodontitis - Plants Cause Disease

block content
    h1 Periodontitis
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/periodontitis/symptoms-causes/syc-20354473") Mayo Clinic]:
    blockquote Periodontitis (per-e-o-don-TIE-tis), also called gum disease, is a serious gum infection that damages the soft tissue around teeth. Without treatment, periodontitis can destroy the bone that supports your teeth. This can cause teeth to loosen or lead to tooth loss.
